cff-version: 1.2.0

message: "If you use this software, please cite the associated manuscript, software repository, and archived dataset."

title: "R code for Hysteresis metrics reveal land-use-dependent stormflow constituent dynamics in tropical Afromontane catchments"

version: "1.0.0"

type: software

authors:
  - family-names: "Tabo"
    given-names: "Zadoki"
  - family-names: "Jacobs"
    given-names: "Suzanne R."
  - family-names: "Breuer"
    given-names: "Lutz"

repository-code: "https://github.com/jluzt2022/mau-hysteresis-reproducibility"

abstract: >
  R code supporting reproducibility of the manuscript
  "Hysteresis metrics reveal land-use-dependent stormflow constituent dynamics
  in tropical Afromontane catchments". The workflow starts from the cleaned
  10-minute hydro-meteorological and hydrochemical dataset used in the study
  for 2015-2020 and reproduces event detection, hysteresis and flushing metrics,
  multivariate response clustering, statistical analyses, tables, figures,
  and publication-output audits.

keywords:
  - hysteresis
  - storm events
  - hydrochemistry
  - flushing
  - tropical catchments
  - Afromontane
  - reproducible research
  - R

license: MIT

references:
  - type: dataset
    title: "10-minute hydro-meteorological and hydrochemical data for storm-event hysteresis analysis in South-West Mau, Kenya (2015–2020)"
    authors:
